[
  {
    "id": "nguyen-thanh",
    "name": "Nguyen Thanh",
    "nameDisplay": "NGUYEN THANH",
    "code": "NT",
    "slug": "artist-nguyen-thanh",
    "born": "1976-04-20",
    "birthPlace": "Quảng Bình, Vietnam",
    "bio": "<p>Nguyen Thanh was born on April 20, 1976, in Quảng Bình, Vietnam. His creative inspiration stems from the beauty of nature, the rhythm of human life, and the movement of society. These elements form an endless source of emotion within the artist, nurturing a continuous current of creativity that evolves with time and the social landscape.</p><p>His paintings capture life's emotional flow through various periods and transformations, reflecting his deep sensitivity to history and human experience. The emotional core of Nguyen Thanh's art is drawn from his love for family, friendship, childhood memories, and the serenity of peace.</p><p>He is particularly fond of the color green — the color of the Earth, symbolizing harmony and life. Through his works, Nguyen Thanh embarks on a journey to seek new light — the light of human existence, of all living things, and of the future of humankind. Light, often recurring throughout his paintings, symbolizes his aspiration for a better, more peaceful world.</p><p>Nguyen Thanh often expresses this belief passionately: \"I love peace; I love the green of this planet.\" For him, it represents the essence of life — for humanity and for all beings. Each artwork speaks a unique visual language, shaped by the ever-flowing stream of time and emotion.</p><p>Nguyen Thanh's works have been warmly embraced by collectors both in Vietnam and internationally.</p>",
    "featured": true,
    "featuredImage": "../images/artists/Nguyen Thanh/2010/mebeo.png",
    "thumbnailImage": "images/artists/Nguyen Thanh/2010/mebeo.png",
    "hasSeries": true
  },
  {
    "id": "hoang-lam",
    "name": "Hoang Lam",
    "nameDisplay": "HOANG LAM",
    "code": "HL",
    "slug": "artist-hoang-lam",
    "born": "1982-01-01",
    "birthPlace": "Hanoi, Vietnam",
    "bio": "<p>Hoàng Ngọc Lâm (born 1982) is a Vietnamese visual artist based in Hanoi. He studied at the Hanoi University of Fine Arts from 2008 to 2013, where he developed a strong academic foundation in fine arts and contemporary painting. Since his student years, Lâm has actively participated in Vietnam's art scene and has been featured in several notable exhibitions, including the Young Art Exhibition (2010–2012), the 18th Red River Delta Regional Fine Arts Exhibition (2013), the Hanoi Capital Fine Arts Exhibition (2014), and an exhibition at Art52 Gallery, Hanoi (2018).</p><p>Working primarily in oil on canvas, Hoàng Ngọc Lâm is known for his textured palette-knife technique, through which he blends figurative imagery with expressive abstraction. His paintings often draw from Vietnamese cultural memory, depicting rural architecture, village life, and ethnic minority portraits as emotional and symbolic subjects rather than literal representations. Solid forms are constructed through thick layers of paint, while backgrounds dissolve into subtle movements of color and texture.</p><p>Through a restrained color palette and calm, introspective figures, Lâm's work emphasizes stillness, identity, and inner presence. His practice reflects an ongoing dialogue between tradition and contemporary expression, offering a quiet yet powerful reflection on memory, place, and cultural continuity.</p>",
    "featured": false,
    "featuredImage": "../images/artists/Hoang Lam/z7481507681916_d7518aab7ff33e7644dd4d4b1ebf0eaf.jpg",
    "thumbnailImage": "images/artists/Hoang Lam/z7481507681916_d7518aab7ff33e7644dd4d4b1ebf0eaf.jpg",
    "hasSeries": false
  },
  {
    "id": "ngo-dang-hiep",
    "name": "Ngo Dang Hiep",
    "nameDisplay": "NGO DANG HIEP",
    "code": "NDH",
    "slug": "artist-ngo-dang-hiep",
    "born": "1962-12-25",
    "birthPlace": "Da Nang, Vietnam",
    "bio": "<p><strong>Ngo Dang Hiep</strong> was born on 25 December 1962 in Da Nang, Vietnam. He graduated from the Hue University of Fine Arts and later completed his postgraduate studies in fine arts in Ho Chi Minh City. He is the former Head of the Fine Arts Department and lecturer at the Central Pedagogical College in Nha Trang, where he trained generations of young art teachers and painters.</p><p><strong>Ngo Dang Hiep</strong> is a member of the Khanh Hoa Provincial Literature and Arts Association and has been actively involved in Vietnam's art scene since the early 1990s. He first participated in the National Fine Arts Exhibition in 1990 and has regularly joined annual Spring exhibitions in Khanh Hoa province from 1990 to the present. In 2009, he held a solo exhibition in Khanh Hoa, and in 2024 his works appeared in a group show at the Ho Chi Minh City Museum of Fine Arts. His paintings have also been featured in exhibitions and art tours at resorts and galleries in Nha Trang and Ho Chi Minh City, where he often appears as a key invited artist.</p><p>Romantic realism is the consistent thread in <strong>Ngo Dang Hiep</strong>'s practice: his main subjects are landscapes, young women and children, rendered with a nostalgic, poetic sensibility. He frequently works with watercolor, silk, oil and acrylic, using decorative color harmonies to evoke peaceful rural scenes, gentle coastal towns and the quiet beauty of Vietnamese life. As the artist has shared, he hopes viewers can rediscover the joy and innocence of their own childhood when contemplating his works.</p>",
    "featured": false,
    "featuredImage": "../images/artists/Ngo Dang Hiep/Ngo Dang Hiep_1.jpg",
    "thumbnailImage": "images/artists/Ngo Dang Hiep/Ngo Dang Hiep_1.jpg",
    "hasSeries": false
  },
  {
    "id": "vu-quoc-dung",
    "name": "Vu Quoc Dung",
    "nameDisplay": "VU QUOC DUNG",
    "code": "VQD",
    "slug": "artist-vu-quoc-dung",
    "born": "1982-01-01",
    "birthPlace": "Thanh Hoa, Vietnam",
    "bio": "<p>Vu Quoc Dung was born in Thanh Hoa province in 1982. He graduated from Binh Duong College of Fine Arts and later from the University of Fine Arts in Ho Chi Minh City. Currently, he serves as a lecturer at Binh Duong College of Fine Arts and is a member of the Ho Chi Minh City Graphics Club.</p><p>Dung works primarily in graphic and mixed-media disciplines, with a strong emphasis on structure, composition, and visual symbolism. His works often explore social themes and collective memory, expressed through a distinctive visual language that balances clarity and emotional depth.</p><p>He has participated in numerous national and regional exhibitions, including the Youth Exhibition (Biennale) and the National Fine Arts Exhibition. His works have been included in charity art auctions such as Operation Smile Vietnam and are held in private collections in the United States, France, the Netherlands, Switzerland, Hong Kong, Singapore, and Malaysia.</p>",
    "featured": false,
    "featuredImage": "../images/artists/Vu Quoc Dung/z7511726081206_7488723efed198595cec1d36985041ee.jpg",
    "thumbnailImage": "images/artists/Vu Quoc Dung/z7511726081206_7488723efed198595cec1d36985041ee.jpg",
    "hasSeries": false
  },
  {
    "id": "dang-hien",
    "name": "Dang Hien",
    "nameDisplay": "DANG HIEN",
    "code": "DH",
    "slug": "artist-dang-hien",
    "born": "1982-01-01",
    "birthPlace": "Hoa Binh, Vietnam",
    "bio": "<p>Dang Hien was born in Hoa Binh province, northern Vietnam, in 1982. She graduated from Hanoi University of Industrial Fine Arts in 2013 and is a member of the Young Artists Club as well as the \"Son Ta\" lacquer art group.</p><p>Specializing in lacquer painting, Dang Hien's work reflects a contemporary reinterpretation of traditional Vietnamese materials and techniques. Her practice emphasizes layered surfaces, subtle color relationships, and rhythmic compositions, resulting in works that are both tactile and contemplative.</p><p>She has participated in numerous group exhibitions in Vietnam and internationally, including shows at the Vietnam Fine Arts Museum, exhibitions in Seoul and Beijing, and specialized lacquer exhibitions organized by the Vietnam Fine Arts Association. Her work represents a continuous dialogue between tradition and contemporary artistic expression.</p>",
    "featured": false,
    "featuredImage": "../images/artists/Dang Hien/dang_hien_1.jpg",
    "thumbnailImage": "images/artists/Dang Hien/dang_hien_1.jpg",
    "hasSeries": false
  },
  {
    "id": "giap-van-tuan",
    "name": "Giap Van Tuan",
    "nameDisplay": "GIAP VAN TUAN",
    "code": "GVT",
    "slug": "artist-giap-van-tuan",
    "born": "1983-01-01",
    "birthPlace": "Bac Giang, Vietnam",
    "bio": "<p>Giap Van Tuan was born in 1983 in Bac Giang province, near Hanoi. His artistic practice is deeply rooted in his emotional connection to Hanoi's Old Quarter, which serves as the primary subject of his work.</p><p>Through expressive use of color and movement, Tuan captures the evolving rhythms of the city—its narrow streets, aging architecture, tangled electric wires, and seasonal changes. Rather than documenting the city realistically, his paintings convey an intimate and poetic relationship with urban memory and personal experience.</p><p>Giap Van Tuan has participated in numerous group exhibitions in Hanoi, Ho Chi Minh City, and internationally, including exhibitions in Canada. His works reflect a consistent exploration of place, time, and emotional attachment to the city he calls home.</p>",
    "featured": false,
    "featuredImage": "../images/artists/Giap Van Tuan/z7511751168183_ebfc75b7046411efb8713bb1639a3c1a.jpg",
    "thumbnailImage": "images/artists/Giap Van Tuan/z7511751168183_ebfc75b7046411efb8713bb1639a3c1a.jpg",
    "hasSeries": false
  },
  {
    "id": "chu-thu",
    "name": "Chu Thu",
    "nameDisplay": "CHU THU",
    "code": "CT",
    "slug": "artist-chu-thu",
    "born": "1984-01-01",
    "birthPlace": "Ha Tay, Hanoi, Vietnam",
    "bio": "<p>Chu Thu is a Vietnamese lacquer painter born in 1984 in Ha Tay province, Dan Phuong district, Hanoi. She grew up in Son La City and currently lives and works in Thanh Hoa province. She graduated from the Vietnam University of Fine Arts and is a member of both the Vietnam Fine Arts Association and the Thanh Hoa Fine Arts Association.</p><p>Specializing in lacquer painting (son mai), a traditional and distinctive medium of Vietnamese art, Chu Thu's practice reflects a deep respect for material, process, and cultural heritage. Working with lacquer and silk, she carefully builds layered surfaces that emphasize depth, rhythm, and subtle color transitions—qualities intrinsic to the lacquer tradition.</p><p>Her works balance tradition and contemporary sensibility, transforming classical materials into poetic visual expressions. Through refined composition and quiet tonal harmony, Chu Thu's paintings evoke a sense of inner calm, memory, and cultural continuity rather than literal narration.</p><p>Chu Thu has participated in numerous regional and national exhibitions, including the North Central Region Fine Arts Exhibitions and the Vietnam National Fine Arts Exhibition. Her continued practice contributes to the preservation and renewal of Vietnamese lacquer painting within a contemporary artistic context.</p>",
    "featured": false,
    "featuredImage": "../images/artists/Chu Thu/z7511677078426_915c60ab66510632b090eef34cdb419a.jpg",
    "thumbnailImage": "images/artists/Chu Thu/z7511677078426_915c60ab66510632b090eef34cdb419a.jpg",
    "hasSeries": false
  },
  {
    "id": "vu-cong-dien",
    "name": "Vu Cong Dien",
    "nameDisplay": "VU CONG DIEN",
    "code": "VCD",
    "slug": "artist-vu-cong-dien",
    "born": "1976-01-01",
    "birthPlace": "Vietnam",
    "bio": "<p>Vu Cong Dien (1976) is well known for his landscape paintings that depict serene and tranquil scenes, with misty twilight reminiscent of a dream. A sprawling field dotted with a few rooftops stretches out, while rolling hills merge with the horizon, forming expansive, enchanting spaces. In this setting, the trees appear peculiar and extraordinary, boasting round or oval canopies that resemble vibrant \"balloons\" reaching towards the sky. Occasionally, an entire forest of trees is mirrored on the pristine surface of a lake.</p><p>In Dien's words, \"I ran towards Nature as if I was looking for a serene harbour in which my mind could roam in boundless grasslands and hilly slopes that stretch to the horizon. I wander in the Nature's Zen realm where I could apparently immerse myself in an ocean of feelings and emotions to taste them piecemeal and then express them in my painting. One day, I suddenly realised that the creator had borne men with all the living creatures, flowers and vegetation to ultimately integrate them into one entity.\"</p><p>Dien's landscapes are not mere reflections of reality; they are his own imaginative creations, brimming with fictional ideas. Whether it's fields or the sky, houses or trees, a single tree or an entire forest, these familiar motifs serve as a canvas for the artist to freely alter colors, experiment with materials, and let his imagination soar. His artworks transform like a vibrant, intricate kaleidoscope—evoking the four seasons, capturing rare moments of seasonal transitions, the enchanting beauty of dawn and dusk enveloped in twilight.</p><p>His artistry bridges East and West: Western impressionism influences his brushwork and oil techniques, while Eastern aesthetics embody symbolic, magical, and colorful elements. Vu Cong Dien graduated from Hanoi Fine Arts University in 2005. Thang Long Gallery has supported him since 2006 with exhibitions domestically and internationally. His works are in high demand in Europe, Australia, the US, and Japan, and are carried in galleries in Singapore, London, Dubai, Hong Kong, Tokyo, Finland, Belgium, and Hanoi.</p>",
    "featured": false,
    "featuredImage": "../images/artists/Vu Cong Dien/z7481523625833_43a7a5352cdf8618b04917c36d137f07.jpg",
    "thumbnailImage": "images/artists/Vu Cong Dien/z7481523625833_43a7a5352cdf8618b04917c36d137f07.jpg",
    "hasSeries": false
  },
  {
    "id": "nguyen-trang",
    "name": "Nguyen Trang",
    "nameDisplay": "NGUYEN TRANG",
    "code": "NTR",
    "slug": "artist-nguyen-trang",
    "born": "1974-01-01",
    "birthPlace": "Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam",
    "bio": "<p>Nguyen Trang (born 1974 in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam) is a contemporary Vietnamese artist whose practice encompasses both domestic and international exhibition contexts. Her artistic career is marked by active participation in collaborative exhibitions and humanitarian initiatives, demonstrating a sustained commitment to both artistic development and social engagement.</p><p>Working primarily in oil on canvas, Nguyen Trang has developed a distinctive visual language that balances formal aesthetic concerns with accessible imagery. Her practice reflects ongoing dialogue with contemporary painting traditions while maintaining connection to lived experience and cultural context.</p><p>Nguyen Trang has participated in charity fundraising exhibitions benefiting underprivileged children, including the notable \"From the Heart\" exhibition with the Ho Chi Minh City Red Cross in 2017, which raised funds for orphans and people with disabilities. Her works are held in private collections internationally, including the United Kingdom, France, Switzerland, Sweden, Singapore, South Korea, Hong Kong, and the United States, reflecting both the accessibility and resonance of her artistic vision.</p><p>Through consistent participation in group exhibitions across Vietnam and internationally, Nguyen Trang continues to develop her artistic practice, contributing to the contemporary Vietnamese art dialogue while maintaining an authentic personal vision.</p>",
    "featured": false,
    "featuredImage": "../images/artists/Nguyen Trang/NguyenTrang_01.jpeg",
    "thumbnailImage": "images/artists/Nguyen Trang/NguyenTrang_01.jpeg",
    "hasSeries": false
  },
  {
    "id": "nguyen-tran",
    "name": "Nguyen Tran",
    "nameDisplay": "NGUYEN TRAN",
    "code": "NTRAN",
    "slug": "artist-nguyen-tran",
    "born": null,
    "birthPlace": "Vietnam",
    "bio": "<p>Nguyen Tran is a contemporary Vietnamese artist whose practice engages with the intersection of abstraction and representation. Working primarily in oil on canvas, his artistic approach emphasizes the exploration of form, color relationships, and spatial composition.</p><p>Through sustained attention to materiality and surface, Nguyen Tran develops a visual language that balances gestural spontaneity with deliberate structure. His works reflect an ongoing investigation into the expressive potential of paint itself, allowing process and medium to shape the final form.</p><p>Nguyen Tran has participated in various group exhibitions throughout Vietnam and maintains an active studio practice. His works are held in private collections domestically and internationally, reflecting a commitment to contemporary painting traditions while pursuing an individual artistic vision.</p>",
    "featured": false,
    "featuredImage": "../images/artists/Nguyen Tran/NguyenTran_1.jpg",
    "thumbnailImage": "images/artists/Nguyen Tran/NguyenTran_1.jpg",
    "hasSeries": false
  },
  {
    "id": "duc-tho",
    "name": "Duc Tho",
    "nameDisplay": "DUC THO",
    "code": "DT",
    "slug": "artist-duc-tho",
    "born": "1976-01-01",
    "birthPlace": "Vinh Long, Vietnam",
    "bio": "<p>Duc Tho was born in 1976 in Vinh Long province, southern Vietnam. Passionate about painting from a young age, he pursued his artistic development through independent study and painting workshops in Ho Chi Minh City. He began his professional artistic career in 2009.</p><p>His paintings focus on rural life and agricultural landscapes, particularly rice fields, harvest seasons, and the daily activities of farmers. Drawing from childhood memories and lived experiences, Duc Tho's works convey a deep emotional connection to the countryside and a sense of quiet resilience in ordinary life.</p><p>He has participated in numerous group exhibitions in Ho Chi Minh City, including charity exhibitions in collaboration with the Ho Chi Minh City Red Cross Society.</p>",
    "featured": false,
    "featuredImage": "../images/artists/DUC THO/DucTho1.jpg",
    "thumbnailImage": "images/artists/DUC THO/DucTho1.jpg",
    "hasSeries": false
  },
  {
    "id": "tran-ngoc-duc",
    "name": "Tran Ngoc Duc",
    "nameDisplay": "TRAN NGOC DUC",
    "code": "TND",
    "slug": "artist-tran-ngoc-duc",
    "born": "1963-01-01",
    "birthPlace": "Phan Thiet, Binh Thuan, Vietnam",
    "bio": "<p>Tran Ngoc Duc was born in 1963 in Phan Thiet, Binh Thuan province, Vietnam. He graduated from Ho Chi Minh City University of Fine Arts, where he received formal academic training between 1978 and 1983.</p><p>His artistic practice spans several decades and focuses on philosophical reflections on belief, humanity, and social structures. Through expressive compositions and symbolic imagery, his works often examine the relationship between individuals, institutions, and spiritual space.</p><p>Tran Ngoc Duc has held solo and group exhibitions at major art institutions in Vietnam, including the Ho Chi Minh City Fine Arts Museum and the Hanoi Fine Arts Museum. His works are held in private collections in Australia, Germany, France, England, Spain, Portugal, and the United States.</p>",
    "featured": false,
    "featuredImage": "../images/artists/Tran Ngoc Duc/z7511666192405_3418a8865d827718ff800d5508281a7f.jpg",
    "thumbnailImage": "images/artists/Tran Ngoc Duc/z7511666192405_3418a8865d827718ff800d5508281a7f.jpg",
    "hasSeries": false
  }
]
